# Security policy

This is the coordinated vulnerability disclosure policy of {{ .Product.Name }}, made by {{ sentence .Manufacturer.Name }}

## Reporting a vulnerability

Report a vulnerability to {{ contact .Security.Contact }}. Please do not open a public issue.

Include, if you can: the product version, what the vulnerability is, how to reproduce it, and what an attacker could do
with it. Reports in {{ languages .Security.Languages }} are welcome.

Report vulnerabilities in the components {{ .Product.Name }} uses to us as well. We pass them on to the people who
maintain those components.

## What happens next

- We confirm that we received your report within {{ with .Security.AcknowledgeWorkingDays }}{{ . }} working days{{ else }}TODO: a number of working days, for example 5 (`security.acknowledge_working_days` in shipward.yaml){{ end }}.
- We tell you within {{ with .Security.AssessmentDays }}{{ . }} days{{ else }}TODO: a number of days, for example 30 (`security.assessment_days`){{ end }} whether we can reproduce it and what we plan
  to do.
- We fix confirmed vulnerabilities without delay, and ship security updates free of charge, separately from new
  features where we can.
- When the fix is out, we publish an advisory: what the vulnerability was, which versions it affects, its impact and
  severity, and what users should do. We name you if you want to be named.
- We ask you to keep the vulnerability private until the fix is out, or for {{ with .Security.DisclosureDays }}{{ . }} days,{{ else }}TODO: a number of days, for example 90
  (`security.disclosure_days`),{{ end }} whichever comes first. If we need longer, we tell you why.

We report actively exploited vulnerabilities and severe incidents to the authorities, as the EU Cyber Resilience Act
requires.

